This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user asked me to "Start work on SYS-581" (a Jira ticket, project SYS, in the `toastboy` Atlassian site). The ticket is a Story: "Refactor: replace game/Outcome.points with GameDay.status enum" in the `next-www-toastboy` repo (a Next.js + MariaDB football league management app). Full acceptance criteria from the ticket:
   - A `GameDayStatus` enum exists with values `NoGame | Scheduled | AWin | Draw | BWin`
   - `GameDay` has a non-nullable `status: GameDayStatus` column
   - `GameDay.game: Boolean` is removed
   - `Outcome.points: Int?` is removed
   - Player points (0/1/3) are derived at the service layer from `GameDay.status` + `Outcome.team`, with no stored value
   - `PlayerRecord` recalculation derives from `GameDay.status` + `Outcome.team`; resulting leaderboard identical to pre-migration leaderboard
   - `mailSent: DateTime?` retained unchanged
   - Cancelled game inference (`status = NoGame AND mailSent IS NOT NULL`) is documented and applied consistently wherever cancellation state was previously checked
   - All existing tests pass with no changes to expected outcomes
   - typecheck, lint, and build exit clean
   No further explicit user messages were received after the initial request — I've been autonomously executing the full refactor per an approved plan, since the session is in "Auto Mode" (per system reminder: bias toward working without stopping for clarifying questions).

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Next.js App Router, Prisma ORM (MariaDB), Zod schema generation via `prisma-zod-generator`, Mantine UI, Vitest (with separate configs per layer: services/components/lib/actions/api/pages/unit/storybook), Playwright E2E.
   - Project layering: Pages → Server Actions (`src/actions/`) → Action Cores (`src/lib/core/`) → Services (`src/services/`, sole Prisma access layer).
   - Prisma migration workflow: normally `npm run migrate` (`prisma migrate dev`), but here blocked by pre-existing checksum drift on unrelated already-applied migrations; worked around using `prisma migrate diff --from-config-datasource --to-schema <file> --script` to get raw DDL, then hand-built the migration folder, applied via `prisma migrate deploy` (bypasses the interactive shadow-DB drift check that `migrate dev` performs).
   - Derived-value architecture: replacing a stored `Outcome.points` column with a pure function `getPlayerPoints(status: GameDayStatus, team: TeamName | null): PointsValue | null` computed at read time in service methods and attached to DTOs.
   - Data migration correctness verification technique: replicate the OLD inference logic (`pickTeamPoints`/unanimity check) in a throwaway TS script, run it against the production `db-snapshot/*.json` files, and diff against the NEW backfill formula — used to validate the SQL migration before trusting it (zero mismatches found across 930 decided game days).
   - Prisma driver adapter pattern (`@prisma/adapter-mariadb`) and the project's `prisma/prisma.ts` singleton with `server-only` guard — required constructing throwaway scripts carefully (couldn't just `require` the generated client without a driver adapter or without a `DATABASE_URL`).
   - Forking (`Agent` tool with `subagent_type: "fork"`) — used to delegate 4 large, mechanical test-file migrations in parallel (GameDay.vitest.spec.ts, Outcome.vitest.spec.ts, Player.vitest.spec.ts, PlayerRecord.vitest.spec.ts) since forks inherit full conversation context and share prompt cache, avoiding re-deriving the whole migration's context from scratch and keeping large mechanical diffs out of the main context window.
   - Project's finalisation checklist (from CLAUDE.md): `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint` (fix via `lint:fix` then re-check), `npm run format:check` (fix via `format` then re-check), `npx knip`, and `op run --env-file ./.env -- npm run build`, all must exit 0 with zero errors/warnings before reporting done.
   - `.claude/worktrees/*` — discovered to contain stale/leftover copies of the repo from prior isolated agent sessions; explicitly identified as out of scope and left untouched.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   **Plan file**: `/Users/toastboy/.claude/plans/dapper-giggling-koala.md` — the full approved implementation plan (context, data model, migration approach, derivation utility design, layer-by-layer changes, order of execution, verification steps). Not edited during implementation, but referenced throughout as the source of truth for design decisions.

   **`prisma/schema.prisma`**:
   - Added `enum GameDayStatus { NoGame Scheduled AWin Draw BWin }` (placed right after `enum TeamName`).
   - `GameDay.game: Boolean @default(true)` → `GameDay.status: GameDayStatus @default(Scheduled)`.
   - Removed `Outcome.points: Int?` entirely.
   - IMPORTANT: `npx prisma format` reformats the WHOLE file to 2-space indent (project uses 4-space) — had to `git checkout -- prisma/schema.prisma` and redo edits manually with exact alignment preserved, never run `prisma format` again.

   **`prisma/migrations/20260816204037_gameday_status/migration.sql`** (new file, hand-built):
   ```sql
   -- Add the new status column as nullable so it can be backfilled before the
   -- NOT NULL constraint is enforced.
   ALTER TABLE `GameDay` ADD COLUMN `status` ENUM('NoGame', 'Scheduled', 'AWin', 'Draw', 'BWin') NULL;

   -- Backfill GameDay.status from the columns it replaces: ...
   UPDATE `GameDay` gd
   LEFT JOIN (
       SELECT
           `gameDayId`,
           MAX(CASE WHEN `team` = 'A' THEN `points` END) AS `aPoints`,
           MAX(CASE WHEN `team` = 'B' THEN `points` END) AS `bPoints`
       FROM `Outcome`
       GROUP BY `gameDayId`
   ) o ON o.`gameDayId` = gd.`id`
   SET gd.`status` = CASE
       WHEN gd.`game` = FALSE THEN 'NoGame'
       WHEN o.`aPoints` = 3 AND o.`bPoints` = 0 THEN 'AWin'
       WHEN o.`aPoints` = 0 AND o.`bPoints` = 3 THEN 'BWin'
       WHEN o.`aPoints` = 1 AND o.`bPoints` = 1 THEN 'Draw'
       ELSE 'Scheduled'
   END;

   ALTER TABLE `GameDay` MODIFY COLUMN `status` ENUM('NoGame', 'Scheduled', 'AWin', 'Draw', 'BWin') NOT NULL DEFAULT 'Scheduled';
   ALTER TABLE `GameDay` DROP COLUMN `game`;
   ALTER TABLE `Outcome` DROP COLUMN `points`;
   ```
   Applied via `npx prisma migrate deploy` (verified: `Applying migration 20260816204037_gameday_status` succeeded). Verified backfill counts against dev DB (345 NoGame / 51 Scheduled / 433 AWin / 53 Draw / 444 BWin = 1326 total) and independently against `db-snapshot/GameDay.json`+`Outcome.json` using the old unanimity-based winner logic — zero mismatches.

   **`src/lib/gameResult.ts`** (fully rewritten):
   ```ts
   import type { GameDayStatus, TeamName } from 'prisma/zod/schemas';
   import type { PointsValue } from '@/types/Points';

   export type GameWinner = TeamName | 'draw' | null;
   export type TeamResultState = 'win' | 'loss' | 'draw' | 'unset';

   export const getGameWinnerFromStatus = (status: GameDayStatus): GameWinner => {
       switch (status) {
           case 'AWin': return 'A';
           case 'BWin': return 'B';
           case 'Draw': return 'draw';
           default: return null;
       }
   };

   export const getPlayerPoints = (
       status: GameDayStatus,
       team: TeamName | null,
   ): PointsValue | null => {
       if (team === null) return null;
       switch (status) {
           case 'AWin': return team === 'A' ? 3 : 0;
           case 'BWin': return team === 'B' ? 3 : 0;
           case 'Draw': return 1;
           default: return null;
       }
   };

   export const isGame = (status: GameDayStatus): boolean => status !== 'NoGame';

   export const getTeamResultState = (team: TeamName, winner: GameWinner): TeamResultState => {
       if (winner === null) return 'unset';
       if (winner === 'draw') return 'draw';
       if (winner === team) return 'win';
       return 'loss';
   };
   ```
   Deleted the old `pickTeamPoints` and team-array-based `getGameWinnersFromTeams`. Rewrote `src/lib/gameResult.vitest.spec.ts` to match (tests for each new export). Ran via `vitest.lib.config.ts` — passed.

   **Types layer**:
   - `src/types/GameDayStrictSchema.ts`: `game: z.boolean().optional()` → `status: GameDayStatusSchema.optional()` in both `GameDayCreateStrictFields`/`GameDayUpdateStrictFields`; added import `import { GameDayStatusSchema } from 'prisma/zod/schemas/enums/GameDayStatus.schema';`.
   - `src/types/OutcomeStrictSchema.ts`: removed `points: PointsSchema.nullish()` and the now-unused `PointsSchema` import.
   - `src/types/OutcomePlayerType.ts`: added `points: PointsSchema.nullable()` to the `.extend()`.
   - `src/types/TeamPlayerType.ts`: `outcome: OutcomeSchema` → `outcome: OutcomeSchema.extend({ points: PointsSchema.nullable() })`.
   - `src/types/PlayerFormType.ts`: added `points: PointsSchema.nullable()` to the `.extend()`.
   - `src/types/Points.ts`, `src/types/TurnoutType.ts`: unchanged.

   **`src/services/GameDay/GameDay.ts`**: every `game: true` → `status: { not: 'NoGame' }`; `getGamesCancelled`'s `game: false` → `status: 'NoGame'` (kept alongside `mailSent: {not:null}`); `getAll()`'s filter param renamed `game?: boolean` → `status?: GameDayStatus`, passed straight into `GameDayWhereInputObjectSchema.parse`. Updated JSDoc comments accordingly. Added `GameDayStatus` to the `prisma/zod/schemas` import.

   **`src/services/Outcome/Outcome.ts`** (most extensively rewritten service, ~940 lines):
   - Added imports: `import { getPlayerPoints, isGame } from '@/lib/gameResult';` and `import type { PointsValue } from '@/types/Points';`.
   - `getLastPlayed()`: `points: {not:null}` → `team: {not: null}, gameDay: { status: { in: ['AWin','BWin','Draw'] } }`.
   - `getTurnout()`: added `game: isGame(gameDay.status)` to the spread result (since `Turnout.game` is a hand-written boolean consumed by `getTurnoutByYear`); `cancelled: gameDay.mailSent !== null && !gameDay.game` → `cancelled: gameDay.mailSent !== null && gameDay.status === 'NoGame'`.
   - `getByGameDay(gameDayId, team?)`: now fetches `include: { player: true, gameDay: { select: { status: true } } }` and maps `points: getPlayerPoints(gameDay.status, outcome.team)` into each returned row.
   - `getAdminByGameDay(gameDayId)`: now does `Promise.all([gameDayService.get(...), prisma.player.findMany(...)])`, uses `status = gameDay?.status ?? 'NoGame'`, and sets `points: getPlayerPoints(status, outcome.team)` on the real-outcome branch (synthetic no-outcome branch keeps literal `points: null`).
   - `getTeamPlayersByGameDay(gameDayId, team, formHistory)`: `include: { gameDay: true, player: {...} }` added at top level; nested form-history filter changed from `points: {not:null}` to `team: {not: null}, gameDay: { status: { in: ['AWin','BWin','Draw'] } }`; `actualForm` entries now mapped to attach `points: getPlayerPoints(formGameDay.status, formOutcome.team)`; the "current" `outcome` object also gets `points: getPlayerPoints(gameDay.status, outcome.team)` attached before `TeamPlayerSchema.parse`. Updated JSDoc ("Uses only prior outcomes with non-null points" → "with a team assigned on a decided game day").
   - `getHistoryByPlayer(...)`: replaced the old 3-query pattern (`gameDay: {game:true,...}` outcome query + two separate `gameDayService.getAll({game:false/true,...})` calls) with a 2-query pattern: one outcome query filtering `gameDay: { status: { not: 'NoGame' }, ...dateFilter }`, and ONE unfiltered `gameDayService.getAll({ fromDate, beforeDate })` call whose results are then split client-side via `.filter(gd => !isGame(gd.status))` / `.filter(gd => isGame(gd.status))` into `noGameDays`/`allGameDays`. The raw outcomes are mapped to attach `points: getPlayerPoints(o.gameDay.status, o.team)` before merging with synthetic entries. Updated JSDoc comments (`game = false` → `status = NoGame`).
   - `getRecentGamePoints(gameDayId, playerId)`: kept the `team: {not: null}` filter (IMPORTANT correction I made after initially assuming a status-decided filter was needed — the original legacy behavior includes rows with a team but undecided game, counting as a "recent game" with points 0 via `?? 0` in `getRecentAverage`, NOT backfilled with 1.45; changed `select: { points: true }` → `select: { team: true, gameDay: { select: { status: true } } }`, and the return maps via `getPlayerPoints(outcome.gameDay.status, outcome.team)`.
   - `getPlayerGamesPlayed`/`getPlayerGamesPlayedBeforeGameDay`: unchanged (never touched `points`).
   - `getGamesPlayedByPlayer(playerId, year, untilGameDayId)`: `points: {not:null}` → `team: {not:null}`, added `status: {in:['AWin','BWin','Draw']}` merged into the existing `gameDay: {...}` where clause.
   - `getLatestGamePlayedByYear(year)`: restructured so `gameDay: { status: {in:[...]}, ...(year condition) }` is always present (previously the `gameDay` filter was conditionally omitted entirely when `year===0`).
   - `getByBibs({year})`: fully simplified — no longer touches `Outcome` at all; now `gameDays.reduce(...)` over `gameDayService.getAll()`, checking `gameDay.status==='Draw'` for draws and comparing `gameDay.bibs` against `gameDay.status==='AWin'/'BWin'` via a `bibsTeamWon` boolean for won/lost.
   - `getByPlayer(playerId)`: return type changed from `Promise<OutcomeType[]>` to `Promise<(OutcomeType & { points: PointsValue | null })[]>`; now includes `gameDay: {select:{status:true}}` and maps `points: getPlayerPoints(gameDay.status, outcome.team)`.

   **`src/services/PlayerRecord/PlayerRecord.ts`**:
   - Added `import { getPlayerPoints } from '@/lib/gameResult';` and `GameDayStatus` to the `prisma/zod/schemas` import.
   - `getAllYears()`: both `game: true` occurrences (main query + `completed` sub-query) → `status: { not: 'NoGame' }`.
   - `upsertForGameDay(gameDayId?)`: now does `const allGameDays = await gameDayService.getAll(); const statusById = new Map(allGameDays.map(gd => [gd.id, gd.status]));` before filtering `gameDays` down to the requested one; passes `statusById` as an extra trailing arg to both `calculateYearPlayerRecords` calls.
   - `upsertFromGameDay(gameDayId)`: similarly fetches `allGameDays` unconditionally (replacing the old `gameDayService.getAll({fromDate: fromGameDay.date})` DB-side filter with `allGameDays.filter(gd => gd.date >= fromGameDay.date).filter(gd => gd.date <= today)` in JS, since the full table is needed anyway to build `statusById` covering outcomes from earlier in the year); builds `statusById` the same way; threads it through.
   - `calculateYearPlayerRecords(...)`: gained a trailing `statusById: Map<number, GameDayStatus>` param, passed through to `calculatePlayerRecord`.
   - `calculatePlayerRecord(year, gameDay, yearOutcomes, outcome, statusById)`: added `const pointsOf = (o: OutcomeType) => getPlayerPoints(statusById.get(o.gameDayId)!, o.team ?? null);` and replaced every `o.points`/`pointsOf` read (`playerYearPlayedOutcomes` filter, `.won`/`.drawn`/`.lost` filters, `totalPoints` reduce) with calls to `pointsOf(o)`.

   **`src/services/Player/Player.ts`**:
   - Added imports: `import type { Prisma } from 'prisma/generated/client';`, `import type { GameDayStatus } from 'prisma/zod/schemas';`, `import { getPlayerPoints } from '@/lib/gameResult';`.
   - Added a module-level helper:
     ```ts
     const outcomeWhereForPoints = (
         points: PointsValue | undefined,
         gameDayWhere: Prisma.GameDayWhereInput = {},
     ): Prisma.OutcomeWhereInput => {
         if (points === undefined) {
             return { team: { not: null }, gameDay: { status: { in: ['AWin', 'BWin', 'Draw'] }, ...gameDayWhere } };
         }
         if (points === 1) {
             return { gameDay: { status: 'Draw', ...gameDayWhere } };
         }
         const winningStatus: GameDayStatus = points === 3 ? 'AWin' : 'BWin';
         const losingStatus: GameDayStatus = points === 3 ? 'BWin' : 'AWin';
         return {
             OR: [
                 { team: 'A', gameDay: { status: winningStatus, ...gameDayWhere } },
                 { team: 'B', gameDay: { status: losingStatus, ...gameDayWhere } },
             ],
         };
     };
     ```
   - `getAll(options?)`: `outcomes` include now also has `gameDay: { select: { status: true } }`; destructures `outcomes: rawOutcomes` and maps to `outcomes` with `points: getPlayerPoints(gameDay.status, outcome.team)` before the existing `gamesPlayed`/`gamesWon`/etc. filters (which read `.points` unchanged).
   - `getForm(playerId, gameDayId, history)`: `where` now spreads `...outcomeWhereForPoints(undefined)` instead of `points: {not:null}`; return now maps outcomes to attach `points: getPlayerPoints(outcome.gameDay.status, outcome.team)`.
