   **`.claude/worktrees/*`** — 5 stale worktree directories found containing pre-refactor copies of many files; explicitly identified as out-of-scope leftovers from prior sessions and NOT touched.

4. Errors and fixes:
   - **`npx prisma format` reformats whole file to 2-space indent**: caused a huge unwanted diff (579 lines changed) unrelated to my edit. Fixed by `git checkout -- prisma/schema.prisma` to revert, then manually re-applying the 3 targeted edits (enum addition, GameDay field, Outcome field removal) preserving the original 4-space style, verified via `git diff --stat` showing only 15 insertions/8 deletions.
   - **`npx prisma migrate dev --create-only` blocked by pre-existing checksum drift**: two already-applied migrations (`20260214092836_add_game_cost`, `20260316000000_add_gameday_hall_cost`) were "modified after applied", and Prisma refused to proceed without `migrate reset` (destructive, drops all dev data — avoided per safety policy without explicit permission). Root-caused via `prisma migrate status` (showed "Database schema is up to date!" — confirming the actual DB state was fine, just the checksum bookkeeping was stale, a pre-existing condition unrelated to my change). Worked around using `prisma migrate diff --from-config-datasource --to-schema prisma/schema.prisma --script` (note: had to also discover `--from-schema-datasource` was removed in this Prisma version, replaced by `--from-config-datasource` combined with `prisma.config.ts`) to get the raw DDL without touching migration history, then hand-built the migration folder and applied via `prisma migrate deploy` (production-style apply, no shadow-DB drift check) — succeeded cleanly.
   - **`node -e` / `require('./prisma/generated/client')` failures**: initial attempts to query the dev DB via a Node script failed multiple ways — `Cannot find module` (generated client is TS source, not compiled JS; needed `npx tsx`), `server-only` guard error (importing the app's `prisma/prisma.ts` singleton from a plain script triggers the Client-Component guard), `PrismaClientInitializationError: ... driver adapter is required` (had to explicitly construct `new PrismaMariaDb(process.env.DATABASE_URL!)` and pass as `adapter` to `new PrismaClient({adapter})`, mirroring `prisma/prisma.ts`'s pattern), and module-resolution failures when the script lived outside the project's `node_modules` tree (scratchpad dir) — fixed by placing the temporary script directly in the project root (`tmp-check-status.ts` etc.) so Node's module resolution found `node_modules` correctly. All temp scripts were deleted afterward (`rm -f tmp-check-status.ts tmp-verify-backfill.ts tmp-check-scheduled.ts` and the scratchpad copy), confirmed via `git status --short` showing only the schema.prisma change and the new migration folder as pending at that point.
   - **`getRecentGamePoints` semantic mistake (self-caught before committing to it)**: I initially assumed ALL "existence check" style `points: {not:null}` filters should become `team:{not:null} AND gameDay.status decided`, but on closer reading of `getRecentGamePoints`'s original code (`where: {..., team: {not: null}}`, no points filter at all, `select: {points: true}` — meaning it INCLUDED rows with a team but an undecided game, treating them as points=null which `getRecentAverage` then treats as `?? 0` rather than backfilling with 1.45) — corrected my plan on the fly to preserve exactly this original (subtly different) behavior rather than applying the blanket pattern.
   - **`OutcomePlayerType` misuse for `getByPlayer`**: initially added `player: true` to the include and changed return type to `OutcomePlayerType[]`, but realized this method's only caller (`downloadmydata/page.tsx`) doesn't need `player` data (already fetched separately) — corrected to an inline intersection type `(OutcomeType & { points: PointsValue | null })[]` instead, removing the unnecessary `player: true` include.
   - **`getLastResult`'s destructure-and-remerge TS union error**: initial approach destructured `{ gameDay: pointsGameDayFilter, ...pointsFilter } = outcomeWhereForPoints(validatedPoints)` then spread `gameDay: { ...pointsGameDayFilter, date: {...} }` — hit `Type '{gte,lt}' is not assignable to type 'undefined'` because `pointsGameDayFilter`'s inferred type was a broad Prisma relation-filter union where one branch didn't declare a `date` field, and TS couldn't reconcile adding `date` across all union members. Fixed by refactoring `outcomeWhereForPoints` to accept an optional second `gameDayWhere: Prisma.GameDayWhereInput` param merged internally at each return site, eliminating the need to destructure/remerge at the call site entirely, and explicitly typing the helper's own return as `Prisma.OutcomeWhereInput`.
   - **`Outcome.ts`'s `getByBibs` string-concat cleverness**: first draft used `gameDay.status === gameDay.bibs + 'Win'` (works but relies on implicit string coercion, against project's "no cleverness" style) — self-corrected to an explicit `bibsTeamWon = (bibs==='A'&&status==='AWin') || (bibs==='B'&&status==='BWin')` boolean.
   - **Lib test suite run surfaced 2 failures I'd missed** (`createMoreGameDays.vitest.spec.ts`, `updateInvoiceGameDays.vitest.spec.ts`): both asserted `gameDayService.update`/`.create` were called with `game: true/false` instead of the new `status:` value. Fixed both (updated expected call-arg objects + one test description). Re-ran: all lib tests (419) passed.
